-- title:
--   Bordered form at mu = 0 on the energy fiber is a degree-two trigonometric polynomial
-- statement:
--   At $\mu = 0$, on the fiber $K_{0,c}(s) = 0$, write $Z = |z|^2$, $u = z_1^2 - z_2^2$, and $v = (x, y) = (w_1 - 2Zz_2,\; w_2 + 2Zz_1)$, so that $w = v + (2Zz_2, -2Zz_1)$. Put $\rho = x^2 + y^2$. Then the bordered form $B(s) = \nabla K^{\mathsf T}\operatorname{adj}(\operatorname{Hess}K)\,\nabla K$ of $K = K_{0,c}$ satisfies
--   $$B(s) = \bigl(c_0 - 32u\rho^2\bigr) + \beta_1 x + \beta_2 y + (-32u\rho)\,(x^2 - y^2) + 2\,(-64 z_1 z_2 \rho)\,x y,$$
--   with explicit polynomials $c_0, \beta_1, \beta_2$ in $(z_1, z_2, c)$.
--
--   So on the fiber, $B$ is a trigonometric polynomial of degree two in the momentum angle $v/|v|$, whose second-harmonic amplitude is $32Z\rho^2$. This is the Levi-Civita instance of the harmonic decomposition in Grisa, *Exact fiber elimination for the Levi–Civita convexity gates*, 2026 (Lemmas 3.4–3.5). There the gate $D$ equals $4B$ and $F = \rho$.
--
--   **Formalization note.** The fiber condition is stated as the vanishing of the polynomial part of $K_{\mu,c}$, which at $\mu = 0$ is all of $K_{0,c}$. At $\mu = 0$ this is $K = \tfrac12(\rho - R)$ with $R = 1 - 2cZ + 4Z^3$.
-- source:
--   Levi-Civita instance of the harmonic decomposition in Grisa, Exact fiber elimination for the Levi–Civita convexity gates of the planar restricted three-body problem, Zenodo 21270420 (2026), Lemmas 3.4–3.5.

